sequenceDiagram
    %% LLM gateway request path — single completion request from caller to backend and back.

    actor Caller as Client<br/>(SDK / curl)
    participant Ingress as Traefik ingress<br/>(k3s)
    participant FastAPI as FastAPI proxy<br/>(:8000)
    participant Auth as middleware/auth.py<br/>(Bearer check)
    participant LiteLLM as LiteLLM router<br/>(:4000, proxy mode)
    participant Cache as Redis<br/>(exact-match cache)
    participant Ollama as Ollama<br/>(Proxmox host, port 11434)
    participant AOAI as Azure OpenAI<br/>(cloud)
    participant Prom as Prometheus<br/>(scrape, async)

    Note over FastAPI,LiteLLM: Credentials sourced from SealedSecret<br/>'llm-gateway-secrets' at pod start:<br/>• BLS_API_KEYS  (gateway inbound auth)<br/>• LITELLM_MASTER_KEY  (gateway→LiteLLM)<br/>• OLLAMA_ENDPOINT  (LiteLLM backend addr)

    Caller->>Ingress: POST /v1/chat/completions<br/>Authorization: Bearer <key>
    Ingress->>FastAPI: route to gateway service
    FastAPI->>Auth: validate Bearer token<br/>(token ∈ BLS_API_KEYS?)
    alt missing token
        Auth-->>Caller: 401 {"detail":"Missing Bearer token"}
    else invalid token
        Auth-->>Caller: 403 {"detail":"Invalid API key"}
    else valid
        Auth-->>FastAPI: pass
        FastAPI->>LiteLLM: POST /v1/chat/completions<br/>(forward body + LITELLM_MASTER_KEY)
        LiteLLM->>Cache: GET cached completion<br/>(exact-match key)
        alt cache hit
            Cache-->>LiteLLM: cached completion
        else cache miss
            Note over LiteLLM: routing_strategy: least-busy<br/>(num_retries: 2, timeout: 120s)
            alt model = local/*
                LiteLLM->>Ollama: HTTP /api/chat<br/>via os.environ/OLLAMA_ENDPOINT
                Ollama-->>LiteLLM: completion
            else model = azure/*
                LiteLLM->>AOAI: HTTPS /openai/deployments/...
                AOAI-->>LiteLLM: completion
            end
            LiteLLM->>Cache: SET completion (TTL=3600s)
        end
        LiteLLM-->>FastAPI: completion (OpenAI dialect)
        FastAPI-->>Caller: 200 OK + completion JSON
    end

    Note over Prom,FastAPI: ServiceMonitor scrapes<br/>FastAPI /metrics every 30s<br/>(out-of-band, no effect on request path)
    Prom-->>FastAPI: GET /metrics (every 30s, async)

%% Caption — supports BLS-PLATFORM-ENGINEERING-GUIDE.md §4 (P4 LLM gateway).
%% Shows the full request path: ingress → FastAPI auth → LiteLLM router (with
%% cache-hit / cache-miss branch) → backend selection (Ollama on the Proxmox
%% host vs cloud provider) → response. Three runtime credentials are sourced
%% from a SealedSecret committed to git encrypted: BLS_API_KEYS gates inbound
%% auth, LITELLM_MASTER_KEY authorises gateway→LiteLLM, and OLLAMA_ENDPOINT
%% is substituted into LiteLLM's `api_base` via its `os.environ/VAR` syntax —
%% so no homelab-internal address is committed in plaintext. Auth failures
%% return a typed JSON envelope (401 missing-token / 403 invalid-key). The
%% async scrape edge from Prometheus is rendered separately because it is
%% not part of the request path — conflating the two is the most common
%% diagrammatic mistake on observability-aware services.
